      "title": "Career & Professional Development",
      "description": "Career & Professional Development | Presbyterian College Skip to content Resources For Close Menu Current Students Accepted Students Faculty & Staff Alumni & Friends First-Gen Students Community Apply Info Visit Give Open\r\n                            Search Search for: Open Apply Info Visit Give Search for: Admissions Admissions Why PC First-Year Students Transfer Students International Students Admitted Students Graduate Students Visit Us Academics Academics at PC Majors, Minors, & Special Programs Academic Resources Civil Conversations Heart of Service Center for Inquiry, Research & Scholarship Undergraduate Programs Graduate Programs Student Life Student Life Get Involved Health & Wellness Living on Campus Spiritual Life Career & Professional Development Blue Hose Athletics Cost & Aid Cost & Aid Affordability Scholarships Grants Loans FAFSA Net Price Calculator Student Employment Tuition & Fees Veteran Benefits About PC About Presbyterian College Leadership History, Mission & Plan Justice & Community Wellbeing For The Community Governance & Policies Accreditation Offices & Services News Giving Events FAQs Athletics Directory Alumni Resources For Close Menu Current Students Accepted Students Faculty & Staff Alumni & Friends First-Gen Students Community Career & Professional Development Career & Professional Development Career & Professional Development Career & Professional Development Student Life Career & Professional Development Graduate Ready For Anything Your time at PC will be life-changing in many ways—but most importantly, it will help you shape a fulfilling career for whatever path you choose. Whether you’re discovering your calling or taking bold steps toward your next chapter, our Career & Professional Development team walks alongside you every step of the way to ensure you get exactly where you want to go. 93% Of students from the reporting class of 2025 is employed, continuing their education, or has entered the US Military VIEW FIRST DESTINATION REPORT Student Life In This Section Get Involved Living on Campus Career & Professional Development Find a Job or Internship Grad School Preparation Tartan Threads Employers Faculty Health & Wellness Spiritual Life Learning with Intention Our Career & Development team works hand-in-hand with you to ensure that every step—every class, every internship, every connection—is intentionally leading somewhere. We guide you in choosing a major that aligns with your goals, connect you to internships that sharpen your skills, and introduce you to employers and alumni who open doors to what’s next. Building on the foundation of your liberal arts education, we’ll prepare you to stand out and thrive wherever your career takes you. Through strong partnerships and a personalized approach, we help you graduate with not just a degree, but with a plan—and the experience and confidence to pursue it. Find what you want to study and start charting a pathway toward your goals. Explore Majors Inspired by Many Our Blue Hose go on to make a big difference in the world around them. Read their stories and see where your PC degree can take you . Read my\r\n                                    story Sam Hauff '25 Sam Hauff ’25 made the most of every opportunity at PC—from wrestling to writing. She even wore a Tartan Threads outfit to her job interview, landing a news producer role—but turned it down to accept a Fulbright, proving that anything is possible. Read My Story Read my\r\n                                    story Suubi Mutebi '24 PC alum Suubi Mutebi tackles law school at Howard while dominating on the field—proving champions excel everywhere. From Blue Hose to Bison, unstoppable. Read My Story Read my\r\n                                    story Gabby Brinez-Pardo '25 Gabby Brinez-Pardo ’25 made the most of every opportunity at PC—from leading campus events to interning at a World War II museum in Vanuatu. That internship inspired her to pursue graduate studies. A first-generation student, Gabby says PC’s support and connections changed her life. Read My Story More ways to succeed We’ve built a network of resources on campus and beyond that helps you turn career preparation into action. Whether you’re planning for your dream job, exploring graduate school, or still figuring it out, we’ll provide the tools, support, and guidance to help you move forward with purpose. Internships Connect with internships that help you build skills, grow your network, and gain clarity on your career path. Graduate School Prep Prepare for your next academic chapter with one-on-one advising, application and essay support, and exam prep. Handshake Consider this your digital gateway to opportunity, where you can find internships, full-time jobs, and more. From Campus to Career No matter where you are in your journey, PC gives you the tools, support, and guidance to take confident, intentional steps forward. Learn how to ace your interview, curate your personal brand, and other essential skills to master the modern job market. Turn Potential Into Opportunity The 4-Year Career Action Plan Follow breaks down exactly what career steps to take each year, from exploring your interests as a freshman to landing your dream job as a senior. Land your ideal job or internship with our resume , cover letter , and interview prep services that give you the competitive edge employers are looking for. VIEW THE 4-YEAR PLAN Get started Explore your career potential Discover your career options with our suite of resources. If you know what you want to study but aren’t sure how it connects to a career, we’re here to help you find what fits. PathwayU Start with assessments, then explore majors and careers that match. What Can I Do With This Major? Connect your major with potential career paths. Handshake Explore opportunities, connect with employers, and launch your career. iGrad Start building financial skills, manage your money, and plan for your future. Candid Career Watch career videos, learn from professionals, and take your next step. For Employers Thank you for considering PC as your recruiting partner! Explore our resources and different ways to connect with students who can bring a PC perspective and add tremendous value to your team. Start Here For Faculty Student success starts with you! Explore tools and resources to support your students in their next chapter, whatever that might be. Explore resources Step inside career and professional development Take a virtual tour of our office in Laurens Hall and see where your career journey begins. From one-on-one advising to internship support and grad school prep, this is your go-to spot for turning plans into action. Launch Career Development Meet our Team Our Career & Professional Development team is here to help you make the most of your time at PC—getting you exactly where you want to be! Reach out with questions or schedule an appointment to get started today. Lynn Downie Associate Director of Career & Professional Development [email protected] 864-833-8381 Kim Lane Associate Dean, Director of Career & Professional Development [email protected] 864-833-8379 Resources For Close Menu Current Students Accepted Students Faculty & Staff Alumni & Friends First-Gen Students Community Search for: 503 South Broad Street Clinton, South Carolina 29325 800.476.7272 Contact Us facebook instagram x flickr Quick Links & Resources Quick Links & Resources News Events Directory Athletics Campus Map Living on Campus Academic Calendar Course Catalog Offices & Facilities Accreditation Job Opportunities Justice & Community Wellbeing First-Gen Students International Students Accessible Education Health & Wellness Single-Sign On BannerWeb Brightspace Campus Bookstore Library Online Payment Resources For Close Menu Current Students Accepted Students Faculty & Staff Alumni & Friends First-Gen Students Community Search for: © Copyright 2026 Presbyterian College | Title IX Policies Consumer Informati